# LINE ENDINGS - LF, everywhere, always.
#
# `git clone` on Windows with core.autocrlf=true rewrites every LF to CRLF on checkout,
# and this repo hands two of its files to the ENGINE, which reads them itself. A CRLF
# terminating the final closing brace of media/tng_ships.json is enough for the engine's
# line-oriented reader to reject the WHOLE file: all 51 hulls are then absent from the
# engine while sbs_utils still has every stat, so every headless run, picker and lint
# reports them present. The bill arrives minutes later as
#     MemoryError: bad allocation
# inside sim.create_space_object(), against a line that never mentions ship data.
#
# Measured 2026-08-22: a fresh clone of this repo failed that way and the dev tree
# worked, and LINE ENDINGS WERE THE ONLY BYTE DIFFERENCE between the two installs -
# every packaged file was identical once CRLF was normalized. Autocrlf had also
# rewritten all 41 ships/*.obj meshes, which the engine bakes .paxmesh from.
#
# The engine team's own data/missions/BeamArcTest/extraShipDataAAA.json is LF, and so is
# every ship-data file the engine accepts. text=auto still leaves real binaries alone.
#
# This governs CHECKOUT only. An existing CRLF clone keeps its files until it is
# renormalized: set core.autocrlf=false, delete the tracked files, and check them out
# again. Re-cloning is the same thing with fewer steps.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.mast linguist-language=Python
*.amd linguist-language=markdown

# THE SELF-PACKAGING TRIPLE. An addon a repo packages is named in three places and they
# must agree - `sbs lint` checks it:
#   __lib__.json   what gets BUILT into a .mastlib / .zip
#   story.json     what a FETCHED copy loads out of __lib__
#   this file      export-ignore, so a fetched copy has no source to load INSTEAD
#
# MAST prefers source over a declared lib ("source wins"), which is what lets a clone edit
# tng_races/ in place and run the viewer immediately with no rebuild. A fetched copy has
# no tng_races/ at all and therefore loads the built mastlib named in story.json. Both
# work; they simply witness different things.
#
# maps/ is deliberately NOT here: it is the mission's own content and is not packaged.
tng_races/      export-ignore
media/          export-ignore

# Dev-only: the art pipeline and its staging area. Never shipped, never fetched.
_tools/         export-ignore
new/            export-ignore
